    rdf:value """Sunday, May 24, 1896, Bellevue, Naples
Packed in the morning. Bernhard went to St. Peter’s. Came here. How wonderful is the Campagna! I mean to pass my old age with it in view. 
x Monday, May 25, 1896 
Went to the Museum and Pompeii.
Tuesday, May 26, 1896 
Museum - drive to Posillipo.
- [NOTE the hyphen] Wednesday, May 27, 1896 
Museum, study of Pompeian paintings.
I was rather ill. 
x Thursday, May 28, 1896 <Bellevue, Naples>
Bernhard visited churches, and had a walk with Miss Sellers, while I went to Capri and paid a visit to Frau von der Hellen,  who is living there. I heard all manner of interesting things about the difficulties of starting the English line of boats - Italian camorra - etc. """^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 175 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1895-96> .

